<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="027" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Search result authorization into shared methods (document and record search)</title>
    <phase>1 Read tools</phase>
    <gate>r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api, auth and tenant-isolation; it refactors two security filters and the endpoint row-authorization code, and the REST responses are frozen</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization refactor on the search hot path (scope decision, per-parent and per-record caller access, SPE pointer stripping, PARTIAL_RESULTS); the REST behaviour must stay identical</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits only the two search filters, the two search endpoint files and new search-auth tests; no other Wave 5 task touches them</parallel-reason>
    <deps>009, 020</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, tenant-isolation, refactoring, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Move the access decisions of the two REST search routes into shared methods that take the request HttpContext and the search inputs or results and return typed outcomes. These are POST /api/ai/search (SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter plus the endpoint's NarrowToAuthorized / AuthorizeResults / AuthorizeRowsByParentAsync / TrimToReadableDocumentsAsync) and the record search route (RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter plus the endpoint's AuthorizeRowsAsync). The filters and endpoints then become thin callers, and task 022's MCP search tools call the same methods instead of copying checks.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core endpoint filters, caller-scoped authorization and retrieval access trimming.</role>
  <goal>One owner per search access decision. A document-search method owns the scope decision (entity / documentIds / all), parent and document authorization, the per-row parent check, the readable-document trim, the SPE pointer stripping, the count recomputation and the PARTIAL_RESULTS warning. A record-search method owns the per-row record authorization. Both REST routes return byte-identical responses, and the typed outcomes carry the reasonCodes an MCP tool can return.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      <p>Added 2026-11-25 by the main session after task 022 hit its escalation trigger. Its report found that both REST search routes enforce access inside endpoint filters and private endpoint statics, not in a reusable service. Spec line 275 says "MUST NOT copy authorization checks into tools. Move them to one shared method that REST and MCP both call."</p>
      <p>Document search: Api/Ai/SemanticSearchEndpoints.cs; Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs (about 667 lines). The filter passes its decision to the handler through HttpContext.Items. IRetrievalAccessTrim.TrimAsync is reached through internal static TrimToReadableDocumentsAsync. Per-parent checks call AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(callerObjectId, entitySet, id, callerBearerToken).</p>
      <p>Record search: Api/Ai/RecordSearchEndpoints.cs (private AuthorizeRowsAsync, MaxRecordAuthorizationChecks = RecordSearchOptions.MaxLimit); Api/Filters/RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs (about 320 lines). IRecordSearchService.SearchAsync applies only the tenant filter.</p>
      <p>Pattern to copy: task 007, PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizePlaybookRunAsync. It is a public static method over a private Decide method, takes HttpContext?, returns a typed result with a reasonCode, and reads the caller and token from the context itself, so no token is passed by callers.</p>
      <p>Also task 008: FinanceAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizeMatterFinanceReadAsync.</p>
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/SemanticSearchEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/RecordSearchEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Ai/SearchAuthorizationSharedMethodTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs (AuthorizePlaybookRunAsync / DecideRunAsync, task 007)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/auth/Ai/PlaybookRunAuthorizationSharedMethodTests.cs (method-vs-route parity test shape)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">existing search contract/auth tests: grep tests/ for SemanticSearch*Authorization* and RecordSearchRowAuthorizationContractTests (must pass unchanged)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="009" status="completed">Record-search query construction proof and cache fixes</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="completed">McpToolError reasonCode shape</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The shared methods are the only implementation of the search access decisions. Filters and endpoints bind, call and map; no check is duplicated, and HttpContext.Items hand-off stays only where REST needs it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">REST responses of both search routes stay byte-for-byte unchanged for every case the existing search contract and auth tests cover: status, ProblemDetails, result rows, counts, warnings and stripped fields. The Dataverse access-call sequence and count are also unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The methods take the request HttpContext and read the caller and bearer token from it themselves (as 007 does). Callers never pass a token, and nothing logs it. They fail closed (UserContextRequired) on a null or unauthenticated context; there is no app-only fallback. Document that the principal and the Authorization header must come from the same request.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Typed outcomes carry a stable reasonCode per refusal (the REST codes, or new ones recorded in notes/027-decisions.md) and no ProblemDetails or IResult.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Methods live in Api/Filters/ (as 007/008) unless MCP tools cannot reach them there; record the choice. No AI-internal type appears in a public signature, so wrap retrieval types if needed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md. The PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (+5 MB or more needs justification; 55 MB total triggers a review; 60 MB is a hard stop). No new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push, run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress. Reviews: unified-access-control-r2 (caller path).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
