    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Merge origin/master. Run the existing search contract and auth suites green, and list the cases.</step>
    <step order="2">Extract the document-search decision (scope, parent and document authorization, row checks, trim, stripping, counts, warning) into a shared method with a typed outcome. The filter and endpoint call it.</step>
    <step order="3">Extract the record-search per-row authorization into a shared method. The filter and endpoint call it.</step>
    <step order="4">Write SearchAuthorizationSharedMethodTests: call each method directly, then send the same input to the route, and assert the same status/code/rows and the same Dataverse questions.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the search suites, ArchTests and the build. Measure the publish-size delta and run the CVE check.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory; the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation from plan in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If keeping REST byte-identical requires a filter or endpoint to keep a check of its own beyond binding and mapping, STOP and escalate. Also STOP if the MCP caller cannot obtain the caller-scoped Dataverse read identity the checks need without passing a token.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter, RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter and the private row-authorization statics in SemanticSearchEndpoints / RecordSearchEndpoints are the only owners today. IRetrievalAccessTrim covers only the final trim.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended in place: the filters' and endpoints' own logic becomes callable methods in the same files (pattern: tasks 007 and 008). No new service class unless placement requires one.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Task 022's spaarke_search_documents / spaarke_find_records would either copy the scope and per-row checks (spec MUST NOT; two owners that drift) or call the services alone. The services alone return records and documents under parents the caller cannot read, which breaks must-not-leak.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test, dotnet publish</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs, RecordSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs, Api/Ai/SemanticSearchEndpoints.cs, RecordSearchEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Ai/SearchAuthorizationSharedMethodTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Every existing document-search and record-search contract and auth test passes unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Calling each shared method directly for an allowed caller returns the same rows, counts and warnings the route returns for the same input.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a document whose parent the caller cannot read is removed (with PARTIAL_RESULTS when REST adds it); a record the caller cannot read is removed; an out-of-scope documentIds or entity request returns the REST refusal code. Each matches REST for the same input.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a null HttpContext or unauthenticated principal returns UserContextRequired and makes no Dataverse or search call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep shows each search access check implemented once; the filters and endpoints contain no scope, parent or record check of their own.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (total at or under 60 MB), no new HIGH CVE, and the uac-r2 review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-02 prerequisite (added after task 022 escalated). Two adversarial-verifier passes (auth, tenant-isolation), run by the main session.</notes>

